# Trendify – React Application Deployment

## 📌 Overview
Trendify is a React application deployed to a **production-ready state** using modern DevOps practices. The deployment pipeline integrates **Docker, Terraform, Jenkins, Kubernetes (AWS EKS), and Monitoring (Prometheus + Grafana)** to ensure scalability, automation, and observability.

---

## 🚀 Application
- Repository: [Trendify GitHub Repo](https://github.com/NaveenOVN/Trend)
- Runs on **port 3000**
- Deployed via AWS EKS LoadBalancer:  


---

## 🐳 Docker
- Created a **Dockerfile** to containerize the React app.
- Built and tested locally:
```bash
docker build -t trend-app .
docker run -p 3000:3000 trend-app

Pushed to DockerHub:
nawin28/trend-app (hub.docker.com in Bing)

Terraform
Defined infrastructure in main.tf:

VPC

IAM roles

EC2 instances (for Jenkins)

EKS cluster

terraform init
terraform apply

Jenkins CI/CD
Installed Jenkins with plugins: Docker, Git, Kubernetes, Pipeline.

Configured GitHub webhook → auto build on commit.

Declarative pipeline (Jenkinsfile) stages:

Build Docker image

Push to DockerHub

Deploy to EKS using kubectl

Kubernetes
EKS cluster setup confirmed with:

               kubectl get nodes

Deployment and Service YAMLs created:

deployment.yaml

service.yaml

Applied via Jenkins pipeline:

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f service.yaml

Monitoring
               
Installed Prometheus + Grafana + Alertmanager via Helm.

Configured persistent volumes for Prometheus and Alertmanager.

Grafana connected to Prometheus using:
               
http://prometheus-server.monitoring.svc.cluster.local:80
               
Imported dashboards:

Node Exporter Full (ID: 1860) → Node-level metrics

Kubernetes Cluster Monitoring (ID: 315) → Cluster-wide health


